        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=EX5-033#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for EX5-033 (Mar. 28, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "This effect gives ＜Security A. -2＞ to all of your opponent's Digimon with levels greater than or equal to the total cards in both players' security stacks.  For example, if the total cards in both players' security stacks is 6, then all of your opponent's level 6 and higher Digimon will get ＜Security A. -2＞.",
        "question": "How does this card's [Opponent's Turn] effect work, exactly?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "It means the total number of cards in both you and your opponent's security stacks.  For example, if you have 3 cards in your security stack and your opponent has 2 cards in their security stack, the total security cards will be 5 cards.",
        "question": "What does \"total cards in both players' security stacks\" in this card's [Opponent's Turn] effect mean?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, that's correct.",
        "question": "If the number of security cards decreases, does the level for the targets for ＜Security A. -2＞ in this card's [Opponent's Turn] effect also decrease at that time?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
